{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Sin_15)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Sin 15)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines Bash)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Worked_Out_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Worked Out Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Easy_Geo_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Easy Geo Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Fast_Law_of_Sines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Fast Law of Sines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_VHS_Math_Mentorship\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by VHS Math Mentorship</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_MadMath_(Fast_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by MadMath (Fast Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6_by_SupersonicMan12_IN_ONE_MINUTE\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 6 by SupersonicMan12 IN ONE MINUTE</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is surrounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> externally tangent to the central circle and sequentially tangent to each other, as shown. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93ddbd1332c9425c7f3e0b6e95e4d5e0235a1eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt a + \\sqrt b + c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"23\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24323ad615514d3902fb6720a462f134c52cf8f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642e91c6a60e30080021d4023563463cf3026b32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(12)+linewidth(1)); size(200); real r=2.925, x=360/12; pair O=origin; draw(CR(O,r),black+1.5); for (int i = 0; i&lt;12; ++i) {  draw(CR((r+1)*dir(i*x),1)); } dot(O); dot((r+1)*right); draw(O--(r,0)^^(r+1,0)--(r+2,0), linewidth(0.5)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;,(r/2,0),up); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(r+3/2,0),up); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf0bc9a3b04380f64b5853505aeae4b190479ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Sin_15.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Sin_15)\">Solution 1 (Sin 15)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Sin 15)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the center of the large circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the centers of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> circles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b81a1a88234d7b42df5a67e44bed44735a8313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, A_3, \\dots, A_{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a3b6305878daebeb36c4af67ee36272916d515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e5302f67cb23f0d290e10ff19e2481b3bdaace6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+1, r+1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />, with the angle opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8702f86573c46298cc2f9967fff3df61c19ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360/12 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />. Note that the line connecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> go through their common point of tangency, by definition, which causes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef100258eefc3cb01f88675aaf511c44213fbf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> to have a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Drawing the angle bisector of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degree angle, we split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a3b6305878daebeb36c4af67ee36272916d515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> into two congruent right triangles, each with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080bdd4b53cf3c5d997f0ee91d272b451f0827d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and side opposite the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degree angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From here, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc05adff7018981fef85a6a04982a13c1d69e71c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{15} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"43\" />, which be derived using the trigonometric identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0bef9e221e4ed8710f830a292fb030d6d63ce65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(A-B)} = \\sin{A} \\cos{B} - \\sin{B} \\cos{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"307\" height=\"20\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07df88d01da2af64beea5ada4d492431d914b4cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296124e1d3f289918ca84f72ab134eb6117c0611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In our right triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc1a216981974a8fa05c5d377562588b2ed4de74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{15} = \\frac{1}{r+1} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"213\" height=\"45\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29b96bc697d988f75b95016ae16eaba257bd313d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a874cac993b0e5af8c57a3d84ae2b20684c8e094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" />. Rationalizing, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bb6a8b30fd683b19c084b606256d6b17809935b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Remember <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/37372487eaaa87e417308a76f1c368bcd7506a7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = r+1 = \\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"171\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f81ce319f3ca9e9c72ac32918cb04feaca25f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66c81446a8998e9545cfd33d36c924727ad94fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+2-1 = \\boxed{7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Law_of_Cosines_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines_Bash)\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Law of Cosines Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the center of the large circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the centers of any two circles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e220396bf8f6704ea4a5f1745cc64ce339090b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e5302f67cb23f0d290e10ff19e2481b3bdaace6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+1, r+1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />, with the angle opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8702f86573c46298cc2f9967fff3df61c19ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360/12 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Using Law of Cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e47d77417b86003265a94d9aaa98356f2148679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2=AO^2+BO^2-2AOBO\\cos30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging in the radius yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d12b22b85edccf90e6dd307a43346d00b217f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2=(r+1)^2+(r+1)^2-2(r+1)^2\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"322\" height=\"43\" />. After solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f12b1d2cc66b1ce43d3061c1f89994ecc99a959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Kevin Wang\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Worked_Out_Solution\">Worked Out Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Worked Out Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f5bca9a836d231d6eb65cf815a9da2592321e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=(2-\\sqrt{3})(r+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"24\" />. Divide both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83a7b6934aae4c3a97e4ef02244d277af8cd396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{2-\\sqrt{3}}=(r+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"147\" height=\"43\" />. Rationalize and expand to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/909e4514adf3875fa7a2aff7dc5f268a9cb11b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+4\\sqrt{3}=r^2+2r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41a963596b30fb2985ff30236a6cbeeffa5eb77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2+2r+(-7-4\\sqrt{3})=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"24\" />. Use the quadratic formula to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/59035127f8142398eaba3e0518b2704c1d8d0c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{-2+\\sqrt{4+28+16\\sqrt{3}}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"216\" height=\"46\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/0958dad75191dd5b899afc766b968381af764fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=-1+\\sqrt{8+4\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"163\" height=\"35\" /> (Note: We only take the plus instead of plus-minus because r must be positive). Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a81f7c43bff36bd696d8bcde52b26bdf4a4faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, and then we need to find some a and b such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07fce2ee80e6efd8e53ea08cb106a578a1a0dce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{8+4\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"178\" height=\"35\" />. If we square both sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81425e7436a020f5162ba952b7bb3b2bf22bf7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+2\\sqrt{ab} = 8+4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"194\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08679a65ff0607b390a9b3a853150f1f4290db3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. Plug in our previously found values to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/069b9674061a8ab149fd975ce508a47a4e8657de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=8+(-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Samuel and Jungbin\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1af4f00a653bfc97c1315e3fbb4af157e6a7e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Remark}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We could've also noticed that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e7d5c9076a75552655ea70ea814614da8c661d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot(4-2\\sqrt{3})} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}*\\sqrt{3-2\\sqrt{3}+1} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}*(\\sqrt{3}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"545\" height=\"48\" />, and therefore directly gotten <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e711c66100bf6b318d095065ab9ed45c0e1878d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+1 = \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{2-\\sqrt{3}}} = \\frac{2}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}*(\\sqrt{3}-1)} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"364\" height=\"57\" /> and solved from there.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Easy_Geo_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Easy_Geo_Method)\">Solution 3 (Easy Geo Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Easy Geo Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We connect the centers of the smaller circles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c79965629cf6c6f6e340be9c4b2384f5ef712316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/14053c7784e3aa0158775165fe6309f1cff2fea5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(250); real R = -1 + sqrt(2) + sqrt(6); real r = 1; pair O = (0,0); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, 0, W); pair C0 = (R + r) * dir(0); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, C0, E); pair C15 = (R + r) * dir(15); label(&quot;2&quot;, C15, NE); pair C30 = (R + r) * dir(30); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, C30, E); pair C45 = (R + r) * dir(45); label(&quot;2&quot;, C45, NE); pair C60 = (R + r) * dir(60); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C60, NE); pair C75 = (R + r) * dir(75); label(&quot;2&quot;, C75, NE); pair C90 = (R + r) * dir(90); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, C90, N); pair project(pair P, pair A, pair B) { pair AB = B - A; real t = dot(P - A, AB) / dot(AB, AB); return A + t * AB; } pair foot30 = project(C30, C0, C90); pair foot60 = project(C60, C0, C90); draw(Circle(O, R), black + linewidth(1bp)); for(int i = 0; i &lt; 12; ++i) { real theta = i * 360 / 12; pair center = (R + r) * dir(theta); draw(Circle(center, r), blue + linewidth(1bp)); } draw(O -- C0, black + linewidth(1bp)); draw(O -- C90, black + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C0 -- C30, red + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C30 -- C60, red + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C60 -- C90, red + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C0 -- C90, red + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C30 -- foot30, blue + linewidth(1bp)); draw(C60 -- foot60, blue + linewidth(1bp)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\n</p><p>Note that connecting the centers of the 12 smaller circles forms a regular 12-gon. A regular 12-gon has angles \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45dfeb2354097df93fadcb094bc70858d0dd95ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{10\\cdot 180}{12} = 150^\\circ,\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1abdd58f4c62b9deb0cdb072752ec4d6605b5934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OAB = \\angle ODC = 75^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"15\" /> Furthermore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9a5b8e07b64f67574996ae088f66991343b0d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae9cec50262b55a0d404e0506be97f73c12367a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf7af395721d8d3763eda8dc606bd76d343151b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OAD = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/99598c292ca0534c8b5d6e3703e40cb43edfd439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Next, we drop the perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. This creates a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c8b62c658c4d2cde679951a8b1e450d1b88b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle and two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles. Thus,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4141e7df46fc7b7d356076bfad2cd2773fe42099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD = (r+1)\\sqrt{2} = 2+2\\sqrt{3},\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>and manipulating yields\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f317289233ca544dfbe081251cccfd82753520.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = -1 + \\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6},\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>so the desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26af5446d30dd3368885b0462e5802ef2cf73cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+2+6 = \\boxed{\\text{(C) } 7.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>P.S. I posted the asymptote code here. Anyone that wishes to use it can steal~&#160;:)\n</p><p>~ABC09090927\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Fast_Law_of_Sines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Fast_Law_of_Sines)\">Solution 4 (Fast Law of Sines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Fast Law of Sines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Add a super simple construction to the diagram as shown below (i.e. partition 1/12th of the dodecagon whose vertices are the centers of the circles)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e8225fafe2cfd16e4fd0de22ea305bae2193dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import graph; size(250);  real R = -1 + sqrt(2) + sqrt(6); real r = 1;  pair O = (0,0); pair C0  = (R+r)*dir(0); pair C15 = (R+r)*dir(15); pair C30 = (R+r)*dir(30); pair C45 = (R+r)*dir(45); pair C60 = (R+r)*dir(60); pair C75 = (R+r)*dir(75); pair C90 = (R+r)*dir(90);  pair project(pair P, pair A, pair B) {   pair AB = B-A;   return A + dot(P-A,AB)/dot(AB,AB)*AB; }  pair foot30 = project(C30,C0,C90); pair foot60 = project(C60,C0,C90);   draw(Circle(O,R), black+linewidth(1bp));  for(int i=0; i&lt;12; ++i) {   real theta = 30*i;   pair center = (R+r)*dir(theta);   draw(Circle(center,r), blue+linewidth(1bp)); } draw(O--C0, black+linewidth(1bp)); draw(O--C30, black+linewidth(1bp)); draw(C0--C30, red+linewidth(1bp)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, W); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, C0, E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, C30, NE);  [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\nAsymptote's being difficult with me (or rather I just suck at it) so see that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a541b87a5d096750a7a349f6708c4fa46930bf68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OBA=\\angle OAB=75^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"187\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a085aacc241d20a087f2f33715d27ee42e63520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BOA=30^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> Using the law of sines, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ea0ab2ba66e0bbbbcd758a1ca19ff201700492d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{r+1}{\\sin(75^\\circ)}=\\frac{2}{\\sin(30^\\circ)}=4\\implies r=4\\sin(75^\\circ)-1.\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"41\" />\nWe now just compute\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4655fba4f095472a287f7a662c47f56c346915.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(75^\\circ)=\\sin(30^\\circ+45^\\circ)=\\sin(30^\\circ)\\cos(45^\\circ)+\\cos(30^\\circ)\\sin(45^\\circ)=\\frac{\\sqrt 3+1}{2\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt 6+\\sqrt 2}{4}.\\]\" width=\"672\" height=\"45\" />\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07d4818db12f0aa13766d1b74278f2fa5f1afb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\sqrt 6+\\sqrt 2-1\\implies a+b+c=\\boxed{7}.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"23\" />\n~shockfront99 (asy stolen from ABC09090927)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nR67IIw_kgg\">https://youtu.be/nR67IIw_kgg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_VHS_Math_Mentorship\">Video Solution 3 by VHS Math Mentorship</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by VHS Math Mentorship\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jtgG1OY-rDs?si=Z50z59yaKjHCUhEw\">https://youtu.be/jtgG1OY-rDs?si=Z50z59yaKjHCUhEw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_Continuum_Math\">Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/K_1rVX0c2iU?si=UrsGO8AtcY1n56ZF\">https://youtu.be/K_1rVX0c2iU?si=UrsGO8AtcY1n56ZF</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_5_by_MadMath_.28Fast_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_5_by_MadMath_(Fast_Solution)\">Video Solution 5 by MadMath (Fast Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 5 by MadMath (Fast Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Y6chDBqy1wg\">https://youtu.be/Y6chDBqy1wg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_6_by_SupersonicMan12_IN_ONE_MINUTE\">Video Solution 6 by SupersonicMan12 IN ONE MINUTE</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 6 by SupersonicMan12 IN ONE MINUTE\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dOpO4K-XSVY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dOpO4K-XSVY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Prob